-- Rifts World Book 17: Warlords of Russia, batch 5: the cyborg bodies.
-- Seventeen vehicles rows of class 'borg', with their M.D.C.-by-location
-- tables and weapon systems: the typical Warlord Light Machine and Heavy
-- Machine (printed 108-114), the ten Cyborg Shocktroopers each Warlord fields
-- (printed 116-140), and the Sovietski's five (printed 214-224).
-- See apps/character-creator/docs/surveys/warlords-of-russia.md.
--
-- One-off data script, run once per environment. NOT a migration.
--
--   node scripts/d1-apply.mjs --local apps/character-creator/db/add-warlords-of-russia-cyborgs.sql
--
-- WHY VEHICLES ROWS. A cyborg body is M.D.C. by location plus weapon systems,
-- which is what the vehicles tables hold; Triax's VX series and Free Quebec's
-- FX series are stored the same way, class 'borg'. The playable classes
-- (warlord-light-machine, warlord-heavy-machine, cyborg-shocktrooper and its
-- ten variants) name these rows in their restrictions.
--
-- EVERY NUMBER WAS READ OFF A RENDER and checked by book-reconcile: 17 rows,
-- no figure disagreed. Cache p141, the end of the Demonfist, is a welded page
-- and was read from renders only.
--
-- CONVENTIONS:
--   cost is the Warlord Cost. The Black Market line and the "equivalent
--     elsewhere" figure are in cost_note.
--   mdc_main_body is the bare main body. The 180 (medium) or 280 (heavy) of
--     cyborg armor most bodies may add is in the Main Body location's note.
--   A numbered "weapon system" that prints no damage - a weapon slot of
--     choice, a cyber shield, hand-held weapons - is in the description, not a
--     weapon row. The Warlord Heavy Machine therefore has none: all eight of
--     its numbered items are choices.
--   Each body's punch table is one weapon row holding every line.
--
-- THE SOVIETSKI LIGHT MACHINE HAS NO STAT BLOCK. Printed 214 gives it a size
-- line and a weapon list and points to the Sovietski Soldier and to the Light
-- Machine O.C.C. for the rest. Its mdc_main_body and cost are NULL and it has
-- no locations; nothing is copied in from either section.
--
-- THE THREE THUNDER BODIES (Thunderhammer, Thunderstrike, Thunderstorm) say
-- "see the Heavy Machine described previously" for their damage notes. The
-- nearest one is the Sovietski Heavy Machine (called shot at -3, the brain
-- survives 18 hours); the Warlord Heavy Machine prints 12 hours. The rows use
-- the Sovietski figure and say whose it is. None of the three prints an
-- O.C.C. or a skill list, so none is a class or a variant.
--
-- STORED AS PRINTED, and named in the rows: the Butcher's knuckle punch is
-- +4D4 in its weapon text and 4D6+2 in its punch table; the Ripper's finger
-- blades are 2D6 and its raking claws 3D6; the Ripper leaps 190 feet where
-- the others leap 200; the White Tiger's tri-laser and the Aftermath's
-- telescoping neck have no line in their M.D.C. tables; the Aftermath's rail
-- gun is heavy in its introduction and light in its weapon entry.
--
-- The Avenging Angel's Vibro-Scythe Polearm is one of that body's weapon
-- rows. The book prints no price or weight for it, so it is not a gear row.

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO vehicles
  (slug, name, system, vehicle_class, crew, passengers, speed_ground, speed_air, speed_water, dimensions, weight_tons, mdc_main_body, cost, cost_note, description, source_book)
VALUES
  ('warlord-light-machine-cyborg', 'Light Machine Cyborg (Warlord)', 'rifts', 'borg', NULL, NULL, 'Running: 120 mph (192 km). Leaping: 15 feet (4.6 m) high or 25 feet (7.6 m) lengthwise; increase by 50% with a running start.', 'No flight of its own. Options: Cyberjet Nodes (jet assisted leaps, increased speed, limited hovering) or a human or ''Borg jet pack; no figures printed in this block.', NULL, 'Roughly human, typically six feet (1.8 m); Light Machines range from five feet, six inches (1.7 m) to six feet, six inches (1.9 m)', '250-350 pounds (112.5 to 157.5 kg)', 170, 1400000, 'Around 1.4 million for the Warlords; 2.6 to 3.5 million credits on the open market. The Warlord figure is stored. No Black Market line is printed.', 'The typical full conversion Light Machine fielded by every Warlord''s Camp: a man-sized, man-shaped bionic body (really a 95% to 98% conversion, since face, brain, blood and some organs are often kept) that can still wear ordinary clothes and armor, ride a horse or hovercycle and pass among people. Nuclear powered; no power life is printed. The 170 M.D.C. body adds conventional environmental armor (30-100 M.D.C.), light cyborg armor (140 M.D.C.) or medium cyborg armor (180); heavy cyborg armor cannot be worn, and cyborg armor costs -10% on prowl, acrobatics, gymnastics, swim, climb, palming and similar skills. Bionic P.S. 28-30 does S.D.C. damage, but a power punch or leap kick does 1D4 M.D. At zero main body the brain and organs last 12 hours; 100+ M.D.C. below zero is unrecoverable. Starting slots beyond the two statted weapons: one forearm weapon on one arm in addition to its Vibro-Blade; two hand weapons of choice (G.M. may restrict); one leg feature or weapon on one leg only; a choice of face, and if human either the Type AA-1 Cyber-Disguise or two face/head or eye features; conventional weapons as owned. Blades may be silver plated and chemical sprays may carry holy water. A Light Machine not tied to a Warlord starts with one less weapon, one less head feature and no Gromeko FFI. PARTIAL CONVERSIONS (also called Light Machines, p.108; not separate rows). 55% Conversion Package: one headjack and ear implant, or handjack; Cyber-Link; two sensor/communications implants of choice; reinforced endo-skeleton and body frame 15 M.D.C.; full leg conversion, typical Speed 45 (30 mph/48 km), leap 10 feet (3 m) up or 12 feet (3.6 m) across from standing (twice that with a short run), each leg 60 M.D.C., each foot 15-20 M.D.C.; one bionic arm (40 M.D.C.) and hand (12 M.D.C.) with two weapons each, P.S. 18-20 and P.P. 18-20; lung implants (gas filtration and oxygen storage cell); light cyborg armor 140 M.D.C. or ordinary body armor (30-90 M.D.C. on average). Warlord cost 300,000 credits; North American or NGR equivalent about 850,000 to 1 million. 70-80% Conversion Package: one headjack and ear implant, or handjack; Cyber-Link; four sensor/communications implants of choice; bionic body frame and full torso conversion 65 M.D.C.; full leg conversion, typical Speed 50 (35 mph/56 km), leap 10 feet (3 m) up or 15 feet (4.6 m) across from standing (twice that with a short run), legs 80 M.D.C. each, feet 25 M.D.C. each; both arms 40 M.D.C. each and hands 18 M.D.C. each, each arm with 2-3 weapons and P.S. and P.P. of 20, each hand with 2-3 weapons or features (a wrist weapon counts as a hand weapon); bionic lung with gas filtration and oxygen storage cell; bionic or reinforced skull with built-in language translator and radio receiver and transmitter; light cyborg armor 140 M.D.C. or ordinary body armor (30-90 M.D.C.). Warlord cost 500,000 credits; North American or NGR equivalent about 1.1 to 1.5 million. For both packages further implants are earned as rewards from the Warlord or bought privately.', 'Rifts World Book 17: Warlords of Russia p.108-111'),
  ('warlord-heavy-machine-cyborg', 'Heavy Machine Cyborg (Warlord)', 'rifts', 'borg', NULL, NULL, 'Running: 100 mph (160 km). Leaping: 12 feet (4.3 m, as printed) high or 22 feet (6.7 m) lengthwise; increase by 50% with a running start.', 'No flight of its own. Options: Cyberjet Nodes (jet assisted leaps, increased speed, limited hovering) or a ''Borg jet pack; no figures printed in this block.', NULL, '8-12 feet (2.4 to 3.6 m) tall', '700-1200 pounds (315 to 540 kg)', 270, 2100000, 'Around 2.1 million for the Warlords; 3.2 to 4.5 million credits on the open market. The Warlord figure is stored. No Black Market line is printed.', 'The average Heavy Machine of the Warlords'' Camps: a hulking, plainly mechanical but still humanoid full conversion built to stand in the front line, trading speed and human looks for bulk, armor and guns. It is too big and too studded with weapons for human clothing, armor or most human vehicles. Nuclear powered; no power life is printed in the block. The 270 M.D.C. body adds light (140 M.D.C.), medium (180 M.D.C.) or heavy (280 M.D.C.) cyborg armor, at -10% to prowl, acrobatics, gymnastics, swim, climb, palming and similar skills in light or medium and -20% in heavy; human-sized armor cannot be worn. Robotic P.S. is typically 28-35 and does mega-damage in hand to hand (Rifts Conversion Book One p.25): 1D6 M.D. minimum, doubled for a power punch. At zero main body the brain and organs last 12 hours; 100 or more M.D.C. below zero is unrecoverable. No weapon in this block prints statistics; all eight numbered items are choices: (1) a major weapon forearm on one if not both arms (Mekanikal forearm weapons, multi-weapon systems, hydraulic arm features, or two arm weapons of choice); (2) a wrist weapon of choice in one or both hands; (3) two additional hand features or weapons per hand; (4) one leg feature or weapon per leg; (5) three additional face/head, neck or eye features or weapons (the armored face plate is popular); (6) conventional weapons, rail guns and heavy weapons being favored; (7) blades may be silver plated; (8) chemical sprays may fire holy water. A Heavy Machine not tied to a Warlord starts with one less weapon, one less head feature and no Gromeko FFI.', 'Rifts World Book 17: Warlords of Russia p.113-114'),
  ('sovietski-light-machine-cyborg', 'Sovietski Light Machine Cyborg', 'rifts', 'borg', NULL, NULL, 'Not printed in this entry. Both sections it points to (the Sovietski Soldier, printed 213-214, and the Light Machine O.C.C., printed 110) give a running speed of 120 mph (192 km); they disagree on the leap, so none is stored.', 'Cyborg Jet Pack or Cyber-Jet Nodes are frequent options; no figures printed in this entry.', NULL, 'Human shape and size: 6 to 6 feet, 10 inches (1.8 to 2.08 m)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'No price printed. The entry prints no M.D.C. by Location, attributes, bonuses or cost of its own; it refers to the Light Machine Cyborg O.C.C. section for details.', 'The Sovietski army''s full conversion Light Machine: a human-sized cyborg with human facial features that can wear conventional clothing and body armor, or light or medium cyborg armor. The entry is short. It prints a size line and a weapon list and sends the reader to the Soviet Soldier and to the Warlord Light Machine O.C.C. section for everything else, so no M.D.C. by Location, weight, attributes, bonuses, power system or cost is printed here and none is stored. Beyond the two statted weapons the numbered list gives: (3) one forearm weapon on each arm in addition to, or sometimes in place of, the Vibro-Blade; (4) optionally two hand weapons of choice per hand (G.M. may restrict); (5) optionally one leg feature or weapon per leg; (6) an optional weapon appendage, typically a large or multi-weapon system replacing a hand and forearm; (7) a Cyborg Jet Pack or Cyber-Jet Nodes, both frequent in the Soviet Army. The section intro adds that Light and Heavy Cyborgs prefer the S-500 Cyclone and S-1000 Thunderhead rifles, with the G-21P laser pistol and S20-20 pistol as sidearms.', 'Rifts World Book 17: Warlords of Russia p.214-215'),
  ('sovietski-heavy-machine-cyborg', 'Sovietski Heavy Cyborg Soldier', 'rifts', 'borg', NULL, NULL, 'Running: 100 mph (160 km). Leaping: 15 feet (4.6 m) high or 25 feet (7.6 m) lengthwise without Cyberjet Nodes; increase by 50% with a running start. With Cyberjet Nodes (40% have them): jet boosted leaps double normal running speed; jet assisted leaps reach 100 feet (30.5 m) high or 200 feet (61 m) lengthwise, increase by 30% with a running start.', 'Cyberjet Nodes (40%): hover up to 100 feet (30.5 m) for 1D4 minutes, then lowered gently to the ground. Cyborg Jet Pack (30%; modular, detachable): maximum 250 mph (400 km), cruising around 70-100 mph (112.6 to 160 km), maximum altitude 2000 feet (610 m); powered by an E-Pack (48 hours) or a cable to the cyborg''s own supply (indefinite); after three hours of continuous use 01-50% chance of overheating and shutting down, rolled every 30 minutes beyond three hours; needs 40 minutes to cool; the heavy ''Borg jet pack has 140 M.D.C.', NULL, 'Height 8-9 feet (2.4 to 2.7 m) tall', '800-900 pounds (360 to 405 kg)', 240, NULL, 'No price printed for the Sovietski Heavy Machine.', 'The one standard Heavy Machine of the Sovietski military: every unit looks alike, a broad-shouldered human figure eight to nine feet tall with its own natural or synthetic face, built with speed and free movement in mind and with feet shaped for traction and climbing. Nuclear powered; no power life is printed. The 240 M.D.C. body adds Sovietski cyborg armor: light (125 M.D.C., -5% to prowl, acrobatics, gymnastics, swim, climb, palming and similar skills), medium (160 M.D.C., -10%) or heavy (250 M.D.C., -15%); the heavy suit and its high-tech face plate (an extra 80 M.D.C. for the head) are worn for infantry combat and heavy assault, while in camp or light combat the ''Borg may go bare-headed or unarmored. Human-sized armor cannot be worn. Robotic P.S. 32 does 2D4 M.D. on a punch, 3D6 M.D. on a power punch or leap kick, 2D6 M.D. on a normal kick and 1D4 M.D. on a head butt. At zero main body the brain and organs last 18 hours; 100 or more M.D.C. below zero is unrecoverable. The bonus list also grants W.P. Paired Weapons for the Vibro-Blades. Unstatted items in the weapon list: (3) one forearm weapon per arm in addition to the Vibro-Blade, laser and ion blasters being typical and only 10-15% using Hydraulic or Mekanikal Arms (p.104-105); (4) optionally two hand weapons of choice per hand; (5) two leg features per leg, typically a concealed compartment and a laser rod; (6) carried hand weapons, most often the S-1000, the S-500 or a rail gun, plus one sidearm, typically an S20-20 pistol, with Triax pistols, the Energy Hammer and the Vibro-Sickle also popular.', 'Rifts World Book 17: Warlords of Russia p.215-217'),
  ('thunderhammer-cyborg-shocktrooper', 'Thunderhammer Cyborg Shocktrooper', 'rifts', 'borg', NULL, NULL, 'Running: 90 mph (144 km) maximum. Leaping: 12 feet (3.6 m) high and 20 feet (6 m) across; increase by 50% with a running start.', NULL, NULL, 'Average height 12 feet (3.6 m); width five feet, four inches (1.6 m) at the shoulders; length five feet (1.5 m)', '2.6 tons', 320, 3000000, 'Sovietski Cost: 3 million credits; the equivalent elsewhere would cost 6-7 million. Black Market Cost: N/A; the process is secret and never shared with outsiders or offered for sale.', 'The best known and most numerous Sovietski Cyborg Shocktrooper, a pre-Cataclysm Soviet design for heavy frontline fighting that keeps a fair turn of speed. It is man-shaped with a barrel chest, back missile rack, thick weapon-bearing forearms and heavy lower legs, painted steel blue-grey with black highlights and a red star; under the tech face plate 90% have a synthetic human face modelled on the soldier''s own. Hands are either three-fingered (35 M.D.C.) or two-fingered (50 M.D.C.), and face plates vary by troop division. Nuclear power with an average life of 20 years. Strictly a ground unit: flying is not possible, since the back launcher rules out Cyberjet Nodes or a backpack, though it can pilot suitably large hovercycles and other vehicles. Purpose-built Thunderhammer cyborg armor adds 200 M.D.C. (medium) or 300 (heavy). Damage notes are those of the Sovietski Heavy Machine. Weapon list item 3 is a concealed mechanical arm and hand (usually a Tool Hand, Robot P.S. 18) folded into the right forearm, usable for repairs, carrying or firing an extra weapon but giving no extra attack; the heading and M.D.C. table allow a Laser Rod instead, without statistics. Item 10: hand weapons are carried too, typically the S-1000, S-500A, rail guns or other heavy weapons. The Vibro-Sickle and Energy Hammer are standard sidearms, but not every Thunderhammer takes them into battle.', 'Rifts World Book 17: Warlords of Russia p.218-219'),
  ('thunderstrike-cyborg-shocktrooper', 'Thunderstrike Cyborg Shocktrooper', 'rifts', 'borg', NULL, NULL, 'Running: 70 mph (122.6 km, as printed) maximum. Leaping: 10 feet (3 m) high and 15 feet (4.6 m) across; increase by 25% with a running start.', 'Standard jet pack: maximum 175 mph (280 km), cruising around 70-100 mph (112.6 to 160 km). Maximum altitude 1200 feet (366 m). Powered by a cable to the cyborg''s own supply (indefinite life). After three hours of continuous use, 01-50% chance of overheating and shutting down, rolled every 30 minutes beyond three hours; needs 40 minutes to cool. The jet pack has 140 M.D.C.', NULL, 'Average height 13 feet (3.9 m); width five feet, four inches (1.6 m) at the shoulders; length five feet (1.5 m) with jet pack (4 ft/1.2 m without)', '3.8 tons', 320, 4000000, 'Sovietski Cost: 4 million credits; the equivalent elsewhere would cost 7-8 million. Black Market Cost: N/A; the process is secret and never shared with outsiders or offered for sale.', 'One of the Sovietski''s new, home-grown designs: a supercyborg meant to soak up heavy bombardment, of which only a few hundred exist and are still on field trials. The armor made it slow and ponderous, fine for a stand-up gunfight and poor wherever stealth or agility matters. Greenish-grey with black and light blue highlights and a red star; the Panoramic Cluster Lens eyes give the head an insect look, with a human face under the plate. Nuclear power with an average life of 20 years. A Cyborg Jet Pack is standard, its performance cut by 30% by the body''s bulk, and the rail gun ammo drums ride on the back beneath it. Purpose-built heavy cyborg armor adds 360 M.D.C.; skill penalty is -30% to prowl, acrobatics, gymnastics, swim, climb, palming and similar skills in that armor and -5% without it. Damage notes are those of the Sovietski Heavy Machine. Item 6: other hand-held weapons may be used, from energy rifles and rail guns to clubs and magic weapons. Item 7, additional bionic systems common to the type: Cyborg Jet Pack (standard issue); 25% have one of the hydraulic hand features; interchangeable left weapon arm; Panoramic Cluster Lens; two more bionic eye features of choice; two hand weapons or features of choice; optional Cyber-Shield; optional Head and Neck Collar.', 'Rifts World Book 17: Warlords of Russia p.219-221'),
  ('thunderstorm-artillery-cyborg', 'Thunderstorm Artillery Cyborg', 'rifts', 'borg', NULL, NULL, 'Running: 50 mph (80.4 km) maximum; 25 mph (40 km) when the cannon unit is attached. Leaping: impossible when the cannon unit is attached; 10 feet (3 m) high and 15 feet (4.6 m) across when it is not, increase by 25% with a running start.', NULL, NULL, 'Average height 15 feet (4.6 m) fully erect, 8 feet (2.4 m) when bent over by the cannon unit (about 12 feet to the top of the cannon barrels); width six feet, six inches (2 m) at the shoulders; length five feet (1.5 m) without the cannon unit, 10 feet (3 m) bent over with it', '18.5 tons without the cannon unit, 38 tons with it', 1240, 5500000, 'Sovietski Cost: 5.5 million credits with cannon artillery unit; the equivalent elsewhere would cost 10-14 million. Black Market Cost: N/A; the process is secret and never shared with outsiders or offered for sale.', 'A walking artillery piece and the largest cyborg thought to exist in Europe or Asia: a gorilla-like giant with a twin-barrelled howitzer and mini-missile housing on its back, a short thick neck, a small head with one slit eye, and arms nearly as thick as its legs that lock and absorb recoil. Silvery grey with red markings. A newish Sovietski design; about 1,200 were built and entered service five years ago, used for civil defense (often dug in or in an M.D.C. bunker), combat support and border defense. Nuclear power with an average life of 20 years; flying is impossible. With the cannon unit mounted it cannot stand upright, walks on all fours at half speed and cannot leap, and it must brace on all fours to fire. The unit detaches and can be used apart from the cyborg, which then has no long-range weapon. The housing carries five mini-missile launch tubes on each side of the cannon; no mini-missile payload is printed. A three-man team is needed for targeting and reloading in a prolonged bombardment. The 1,240 M.D.C. main body already includes its heavy armor plating. Skill penalty is -20% on most skills (swim, climb and palming included), and prowl, acrobatics, gymnastics and the like are impossible. Damage notes are those of the Sovietski Heavy Machine. Any Thunderstorm may ask for reconstruction as a human-like Light or Heavy Machine within 48 hours, and the change cannot be reversed. Item 7: giant-sized hand-held weapons may be used, from energy rifles and rail guns to clubs and magic weapons; a Large Energy Hammer (90 M.D.C.) is in the M.D.C. table. Item 8, additional bionic systems common to the type: Wide-Angle Vision with Multi-Optics; two more bionic eye features of choice; two hand weapons or features of choice; Internal Comp-Calculator; Low-Frequency (earthquake) Audio Rig; Sound Filtration System; optional Head Collar & Hood.', 'Rifts World Book 17: Warlords of Russia p.221-224'),
  ('tempest-cyborg-shocktrooper', 'Tempest Cyborg Shocktrooper', 'rifts', 'borg', NULL, NULL, 'Running: 70 mph (112.6 km) maximum. Leaping: 8 feet (2.4 m) high and 12 feet (3.6 m) lengthwise, +20% with a running start (jets and wings make leaping awkward); jet thruster assisted leaps 100 feet (30.5 m) high and 200 feet (61 m) across.', 'Hover stationary up to 200 feet (61 m) high; maximum speed 240 mph (384 km); cruising about 100 mph (160 km); maximum altitude 500 feet (152 m). Jets need to cool after about 8 hours of constant use; unlimited power from the nuclear supply.', NULL, 'Height 13 feet (3.9 m) to the tip of the horns; width 5 feet, 6 inches (1.7 m) at the shoulders, 16 feet (4.9 m) with wings fully extended; length 7 feet (2.1 m)', '2 tons', 340, 3500000, 'Black Market Cost: N/A; the process is secret and never offered for sale to outsiders. Warlord Cost: 3.5 million credits; the equivalent elsewhere would cost 6-8 million.', 'Warlord Alekseyevna''s flying full conversion cyborg: a thick, heavily plated body with a mechanical dragon head, bone-like spikes along the crest, spine and 10 foot (3 m) prehensile tail, back-mounted jets, and wings that fold behind the back on the ground. In service for nearly 70 years, it trades the speed and agility of a SAMAS for firepower and toughness. The broad flat feet let it ski over water, ice and snow (no speed is printed for this). Nuclear power system, average life 20 years. Robotic P.S. 38, Bionic P.P. 22, Horror Factor 11. The optional rail gun needs an ammo-drum mounted behind the head between the wings. Item 10 of the weapon list is an optional Cyber Shield (no figures printed). Item 11: hand-held weapons of any kind may be carried, and many Tempests carry a dozen hand grenades in a satchel to drop or throw like small bombs. The laser eyes aim by line of sight, so the whole head must turn to aim.', 'Rifts World Book 17: Warlords of Russia p.116-119'),
  ('butcher-cyborg-shocktrooper', 'Butcher Cyborg Shocktrooper', 'rifts', 'borg', NULL, NULL, 'Running: 120 mph (192 km) maximum. Leaping (without jet propulsion): 12 feet (3.6 m) high and 20 feet (6 m) across, +50% with a running start; jet thruster assisted leaps 100 feet (30.5 m) high and 200 feet (61 m) across.', NULL, NULL, 'Height 11 feet (3.3 m); width 5 feet, 6 inches (1.7 m) at the shoulders; length 5 feet (1.5 m)', '2.3 tons', 320, 2900000, 'Black Market Cost: N/A; the process is secret and never offered for sale to outsiders. Warlord Cost: 2.9 million credits; the equivalent elsewhere would cost 6-7 million.', 'One of Warlord Burgasov''s two Shocktrooper bodies: a hulking, human-shaped superheavy frame whose head sits recessed behind a metal collar and under a cowl rising from the back, with the shoulder armor shielding it from the sides. The head therefore needs a Called Shot at -6 to strike, while the cyborg keeps clear vision to the front and sides. Nuclear power system, average life 20 years. Robotic P.S. 38, Bionic P.P. 22, Horror Factor 11. Flying is not possible unless a Cyborg Jet Pack is used or the body has the Cyberjet Node package (see the Cybernetics section). Roughly 25% have Cyberjet Nodes (jet assisted leaps, more speed, limited hover) and a Cyborg Jet Pack is issued as needed. Weapon list item 7 is an optional Cyber Shield; item 8 allows any hand-held weapons; item 9 lists common extras: an interchangeable left weapon arm, one additional Bionic Eye feature of choice, and a Hydraulic Ram Arm that sometimes replaces the Vibro-Blade arm. The knuckle claws are silver plated.', 'Rifts World Book 17: Warlords of Russia p.119-121'),
  ('ripper-cyborg-shocktrooper', 'Ripper Cyborg Shocktrooper', 'rifts', 'borg', NULL, NULL, 'Running: 90 mph (144 km) maximum. Leaping (without jet propulsion): 15 feet (4.6 m) high and 20 feet (6 m) across thanks to leg hydraulics, +50% with a running start; jet thruster assisted leaps 100 feet (30.5 m) high and 190 feet (58 m) across.', NULL, NULL, 'Height 11 feet (3.3 m); width 5 feet (1.5 m) at the shoulders; length 4 feet (1.2 m)', '2.1 tons', 360, 2800000, 'Black Market Cost: N/A; the process is secret and never offered for sale to outsiders. Warlord Cost: 2.8 million credits; the equivalent elsewhere would cost 6-8 million.', 'Warlord Burgasov''s front-line assault body, among the most heavily armored of all the Warlords'' cyborgs: it opens with missile barrages, then closes to cut through vehicles, fortifications and bionic limbs. It wears a screaming-demon face plate; the right arm ends in a shielded tri-blade buzz saw and the left in a two-fingered (plus thumb) clamping hand, so it is comparatively slow and poor at delicate hand work. The head, screened by shoulder plates and the rear launchers, needs a Called Shot at -4 to strike. Nuclear power system, average life 20 years. Robotic P.S. 44, Bionic P.P. 24, Horror Factor 12. Flying is not possible unless a Cyborg Jet Pack is used or the body has the Cyberjet Node package (see the Cybernetics section). Roughly 30% have Cyberjet Nodes and a Cyborg Jet Pack is issued as needed. The back launch tubes take one minute to reload by hand. The chemical spray may also be loaded with holy water. Weapon list item 10 allows any hand-held weapons; item 11 lists an interchangeable right weapon arm, leg servos and hydraulics (already counted in the stats), and a Hydraulic Ram Arm or other weapon arm that sometimes replaces the buzz saw arm. The finger blades are silver plated.', 'Rifts World Book 17: Warlords of Russia p.121-123'),
  ('white-tiger-cyborg-shocktrooper', 'White Tiger Cyborg Shocktrooper', 'rifts', 'borg', NULL, NULL, 'Running: 144 mph (230 km) maximum; augmented with hydraulics. Leaping (without jet propulsion): 20 feet (6 m) high and 25 feet (7.6 m) across thanks to leg hydraulics, +50% with a running start; jet thruster assisted leaps 100 feet (30.5 m) high and 200 feet (61 m) across.', NULL, NULL, 'Height 10 feet (3 m); width 6 feet (1.8 m) at the shoulders; length 4 feet (1.2 m)', '2 tons', 300, 2600000, 'Black Market Cost: N/A; the process is secret and never offered for sale to outsiders. Warlord Cost: 2.6 million credits; the equivalent elsewhere would cost 6-7 million.', 'Warlord Kolodenko''s Shocktrooper, built for speed, stealth and infantry fighting: a broad-shouldered, barrel-chested body on short thick legs, armored in white or dull grey with black tiger stripes and a feline face plate. It runs upright but is faster loping on all fours. Its clawed hands have two thick fingers and a thumb yet keep full dexterity for weapons and machines. It works both as a heavy assault unit and as a stealth operative for reconnaissance, tracking and commando raids, and usually carries rail guns or other heavy hand-held weapons as well. The low-profile head needs a Called Shot at -4 to strike. Nuclear power system, average life 20 years. Robotic P.S. 46, Bionic P.P. 24, Horror/Awe Factor 10. Also +15% to climbing and no prowl penalty. Flying is not possible unless a Cyborg Jet Pack is used or the body has the Cyberjet Node package (see the Cybernetics section). Only 5% have Cyberjet Nodes; a Cyborg Jet Pack is issued as needed. Weapon list item 9 allows any hand-held weapons; item 10 lists an interchangeable right weapon arm, Audio-Filter & Enhancement, leg servos and hydraulics (already counted in the stats), and an optional Panorama Cluster Lens or Wide-Angle Lens (about 20% have one or the other). The finger blades are silver plated.', 'Rifts World Book 17: Warlords of Russia p.123-126'),
  ('holocaust-cyborg-shocktrooper', 'Holocaust Cyborg Shocktrooper', 'rifts', 'borg', NULL, NULL, 'Running/Rolling: 80 mph (128.7 km) maximum. Leaping: not applicable.', NULL, NULL, 'Height 12 feet (3.6 m) to the tip of the horns; width 6 feet (1.8 m) at the shoulders, 7 feet (2.1 m) overall including the treads; length 8 feet (2.4 m)', '3.6 tons', 360, 4200000, 'Black Market Cost: N/A; the process is secret and never offered for sale to outsiders. Warlord Cost: 4.2 million credits; the equivalent elsewhere would cost 8-9 million.', 'Warlord Orloff''s heavy combat cyborg: a horned, skull-faced demon-knight torso bristling with guns and riding on tank treads instead of legs, so it rolls rather than runs and cannot leap; no flying line is printed. It and the Aftermath come from alien technology Orloff stole and blended with Earth science, which gives them energy weapons and miniaturization other Camps lack. It normally leads the first assault wave. A second, smaller pair of arms under the main ones (weapon list item 6) works hand-held weapons and fights in close combat; of its +2 melee attacks, one is from those arms and one from the integrated weapon systems. Nuclear power system, average life 20 years. Robotic P.S. 40, Bionic P.P. 22, Horror Factor 14. The shoulder cannon and rail gun swing forward from a locked-back storage position, with a 45 degree arc up and down and 45 degrees left and right. The rail gun can be loaded with silver-plated rounds. Item 8 allows any hand-held weapons; a Vibro-Knife or short sword, one energy pistol and one energy rifle are usual.', 'Rifts World Book 17: Warlords of Russia p.126-128'),
  ('aftermath-cyborg-shocktrooper', 'Aftermath Cyborg Shocktrooper', 'rifts', 'borg', NULL, NULL, 'Running: 100 mph (160.9 km) maximum. Leaping: without jet propulsion 20 feet (6 m) high and 25 feet (7.6 m) across; increase by 50% with a running start. Jet thruster assisted leaps: 100 feet (30.5 m) high and 200 feet (61 m) across.', 'Not possible unless a Cyborg Jet Pack is used or the ''Borg has the Cyberjet Node package (see the book''s Cybernetics section).', NULL, 'Height 14 feet (4.3 m) to the top of the cooling unit, about 12 feet (3.6 m) at the shoulders; width 5 feet (1.2 m) at the shoulders; length 4 feet, 6 inches (1.4 m)', '4 tons', 350, 4800000, 'Black Market Cost: N/A; the process is secret and is never sold to outsiders. Warlord Cost: 4.8 million credits; the equivalent elsewhere would cost 8-10 million.', 'Warlord Orloff''s second heavy Cyborg Shocktrooper, nicknamed Orloff''s Grim Reaper for the chain saw that replaces its right hand. It normally leads the second wave (with Cossacks, Soldati, Light Machines and Reavers) or mops up after the Holocaust-led first assault. A hunchback cooling unit keeps the particle beam cannon and other energy weapons from overheating, so the body is always wrapped in smoke and steam; the unit also shields the head so it cannot be shot from behind. Knight-style face plate and a head collar. Nuclear power system, average life 20 years. Special systems: the right weapon arm is interchangeable; servo and hydraulic legs (their bonuses and speed are already in the stats); an accordion-style telescoping neck that extends the head about five feet (1.5 m) so it can look around the cooling pod and fully behind itself (the neck has 100 M.D.C. and is +1 to dodge; it is not a line of the M.D.C. by Location table); 8% have Cyberjet Nodes for jet assisted leaps, more speed and limited hovering. Optional: a Cyborg Jet Pack issued as needed, a Wide-Angle Lens (about 20% have one), a Cyber Shield. Hand-held weapons of any kind may be carried; one energy pistol or one energy rifle is standard, and grenades or other explosives may be used. Tactile sensitivity 35%; Horror Factor 13.', 'Rifts World Book 17: Warlords of Russia p.129-131'),
  ('avenging-angel-cyborg-shocktrooper', 'Avenging Angel Cyborg Shocktrooper', 'rifts', 'borg', NULL, NULL, 'Running: with wings, 70 mph (112.6 km) maximum; without wings, 130 mph (208 km). Leaping: without jet assistance 15 feet (4.6 m) high and 20 feet (6 m) across; increase by 60% with a running start. Jet thruster assisted leaps: 100 feet (30.5 m) high and 200 feet (61 m) across.', 'Silent glide 10-20 mph (16 to 32 km); silent dive 60-100 mph (96 to 160 km). Maximum speed 340 mph (544 km); cruising 60-100 mph (96 to 160 km). Can hover stationary at any height within its altitude range and float/glide on wind currents. Maximum altitude 12,000 feet (3,657 m), a little more than two miles (3.2 km). Flying range: the jets need to cool after about 8 hours of constant use, but switching to gliding can keep it aloft for days; unlimited power from the ''Borg''s nuclear supply.', NULL, 'Height 10 feet (3 m) to the top of the head; the folded wings add about two feet (0.6 m) for an overall height of 12 feet (3.6 m). Width three feet, 6 inches (1.1 m) at the shoulders; 16 feet (4.9 m) with wings fully extended; eight feet (2.4 m) with wings folded in half. Length 4 feet (1.2 m)', '1.2 tons', 290, 3400000, 'Black Market Cost: N/A; the process is secret and is never sold to outsiders. Warlord Cost: 3.4 million credits; the equivalent elsewhere would cost 6-8 million.', 'Warlord Romanov''s flying Cyborg Shocktrooper, a mechanical angel in knightly armor with feather-styled metal and ceramic wings; the design is eleven years old and replaced a bulkier model that could only leap and glide. The wings belong to a detachable jet propulsion unit, so a wrecked wing can be dropped and the cyborg fights on foot (and runs faster without it). It gives up firepower for speed, agility and silence, gliding in unheard, which earned the nickname Angels of Death. Colors: gold with purple, red or silver trim and gold or white wings; scouts sky blue with white; troop leaders red with gold and black. Bird-shaped helmet, golden human face plate, taloned two-fingered hands and clawed feet. Nuclear power system, average life 20 years. Horror/Awe Factor 12, +2 against the religious or those fearful of angels. Tactile sensitivity 45%. Bonus skills Prowl (+15%) and Acrobatics (+5%). Weapon system 7 is a Cyber Shield, optional but used by about one third. Hand-held weapons may be carried, and many carry a dozen or more hand grenades in a satchel to drop like small bombs. Common bionic systems: Audio-Filter & Enhancement; Super-Telescopic Eye (5000 foot/1524 m range); servo and hydraulic legs (already in the stats); optional Wide-Angle Lens (about 20%); optional one additional forearm weapon of choice on one or both arms.', 'Rifts World Book 17: Warlords of Russia p.131-134'),
  ('assassin-cyborg-shocktrooper', 'Assassin Cyborg Shocktrooper', 'rifts', 'borg', NULL, NULL, 'Running: 110 mph (176 km). Leaping: 12 feet (3.6 m) high and 18 feet (5.4 m) across, plus the distance gained from acrobatic or gymnastic skills; increase 30% with a running start.', 'Not possible unless a Cyborg Jet Pack is used or the ''Borg has the Cyberjet Node package (see the book''s Cybernetics section).', NULL, 'Height 10 feet (3 m) to the top of the head; width three feet, 6 inches (1.1 m) at the shoulders; length 4 feet (1.2 m)', '1200 pounds (540 kg)', 270, 3200000, 'Black Market Cost: N/A; the process is secret and is never sold to outsiders. Warlord Cost: 3.2 million credits; the equivalent elsewhere would cost 6-8 million.', 'Warlord Seriyev''s four-armed stealth Shocktrooper, also known as the Silent Spy and Silent Death. He built it first and uses it mostly as a superspy and commando; it is the one Shocktrooper design the other Warlords routinely copy. Their copies swap in their own camp''s head and face plate, lack the Psionic Electro-Magnetic Dampers, and give up one or two audio or optic features for another forearm weapon or a Mekanikal Weapon Arm. Only 10 feet tall and lightly armored. Each of the four arms carries a different fit (see weapons): the first also has a Wrist Needle and Drug Dispenser and a fingerjack; the third a climb cord and grappling hook and a finger camera; the fourth is a Tool Hand (fingerjack, fingertip screwdrivers with changeable heads, finger pliers, fingertip lights, a retractable drill in the middle knuckle) plus a Garrote Wrist Wire and an optional forearm weapon (about half have one) that may be replaced by a small secret compartment. Psionic Electro-Magnetic Dampers: brain implants that fog psionic probes, giving +1 to save vs all psionic attacks, +2 vs possession and +1 vs magic illusions and mind control; extremely rare in Russia and Asia. Common bionic systems: Audio-Filter & Enhancement (listed twice), Panorama Cluster Lens, Low-Frequency (earthquake) Audio Rig, Modulating Voice Synthesizer, Molecular Analyzer; optional one additional forearm weapon on one or both arms; optional Cyber Shield. Hand-held weapons may be used. Nuclear power system, average life 20 years. Tactile sensitivity 75% for two limbs, 45% for the other two. Horror/Awe Factor 12. Bonus skills Boxing, Prowl (+15%), Acrobatics (+5%).', 'Rifts World Book 17: Warlords of Russia p.134-136'),
  ('mantis-cyborg-shocktrooper', 'Mantis Cyborg Shocktrooper', 'rifts', 'borg', NULL, NULL, 'Running: 120 mph (192 km). Leaping: 18 feet (5.4 m) high and 32 feet (9.7 m) across, plus the distance gained from the acrobatics skill; increase 30% with a running start. With the Cyberjet Node Package (60% have it): travelling by jet boosted leaps doubles normal running speed; jet assisted leaps reach 100 feet (30.5 m) high or 200 feet (61 m) lengthwise, increase by 30% with a running start.', 'Flying not possible. With the Cyberjet Node Package only: can hover up to 100 feet (30.5 m) in the air for 1D4+1 minutes before altitude is lost and the ''Borg is lowered quickly but gently to the ground.', NULL, 'Height 12 feet (3.6 m) to the top of the head; width three feet, 6 inches (1.1 m) at the shoulders; length three feet, 6 inches (1.1 m)', 'One ton', 280, 3200000, 'Black Market Cost: N/A; the process is secret and is never sold to outsiders. Warlord Cost: 3.2 million credits; the equivalent elsewhere would cost 7-8 million.', 'Warlord Seriyev''s second Shocktrooper, a tall, slender humanoid praying mantis painted green or greenish-grey and built as much for stealth, wall climbing and spying as for fighting. Thin legs and upper arms, wide shoulders, a slouching chest, an insect head with bulbous optic and sensor clusters and a biting mechanical jaw. The oversized forearms carry four small jagged Vibro-Blades along the outer edge, a long scythe blade that flips forward over the hand, and six laser slots under the wrist. Three prehensile clawed toes per foot (two front, one back) for climbing, grabbing and carrying. 60% have the Cyberjet Node package (small jet thrusters in the back and legs) for jet assisted leaps and limited hovering. One arm has a Garrote Wrist Wire (Rifts RPG, page 240). About 15% have Psionic Electro-Magnetic Dampers (+1 to save vs all psionic attacks, +2 vs possession, +1 vs magic illusions and mind control). Common bionic systems: Prehensile Feet, Audio-Filter & Enhancement, Wide Angle Vision, Low-Frequency (earthquake) Audio Rig, Modulating Voice Synthesizer, Molecular Analyzer; optional one additional Hand weapon of choice on one or both hands. Hand-held weapons may be used. Nuclear power system, average life 20 years. Tactile sensitivity 45%. Horror/Awe Factor 12. +10% to climbing skill; bonus skills Boxing, Prowl (+5%), Acrobatics (+5%).', 'Rifts World Book 17: Warlords of Russia p.136-138'),
  ('demonfist-cyborg-shocktrooper', 'Demonfist Cyborg Shocktrooper', 'rifts', 'borg', NULL, NULL, 'Running: 50 mph (80.4 km) maximum. Leaping: 8 feet (2.4 m) high and 14 feet (4.3 m) across; increase by 50% with a running start.', 'Not possible unless a Cyborg Jet Pack is used, and even then the normal speed and altitude is reduced by 60% due to its size, bulk and weight. Cyberjet Node systems are useless.', NULL, 'Height 14 feet (4.3 m) to the top of the horns and with the big guns pointed forward, about 12 feet (3.6 m) at the shoulders; width 7 feet (2.1 m) at the shoulders, 10 feet (3 m) in spiked demon armor; length 5 feet (1.5 m)', '7.1 tons', 350, 4200000, 'Black Market Cost: N/A; the process is secret and is never sold to outsiders. Warlord Cost: 4.2 million credits; the equivalent elsewhere would cost 8-10 million.', 'Warlord Sokolov''s Shocktrooper, among the oldest, biggest and oddest of the designs: a walking tank with two shoulder cannons, a gun on each forearm and three long blades over the right hand. A demon face plate with curling ram''s horns and thick armor plates bristling with jagged spines make it look monstrous. Slower than every later Shocktrooper, but its armor (above all with the chest plate, which the illustration omits) lets it soak up punishment, and its strength is legendary. The small nozzles on the chest, waist and back are cooling nodules/release valves, not weapons. Special systems: the body rotates 360 degrees at the hips; two large storage compartments in the left leg; a Synthetic Voice Enhancer for grunts, growls and roars; optional Cyborg Jet Pack issued as needed; optional Wide-Angle Lens (about 15% have it). The left hand also holds a fingerjack, and the right palm a garrote wire for strangling. Hand-held weapons may be used; one energy pistol or one energy rifle is standard, and grenades or other explosives may be used. Nuclear power system, average life 20 years. Tactile sensitivity 35%. Horror Factor 13.', 'Rifts World Book 17: Warlords of Russia p.138-140');

